# The DM modules' deliberate catches of an Error type or Throwable (sync-no-catch-all.sh; Phase 9
# design §16.1, §22.33). One line per (file, clause as matched, whitespace squashed): the exact count
# in that file and why nothing is swallowed. A clause found more often fails every occurrence; an
# entry found fewer times than it says is stale and fails. Only android/messaging and
# android/crypto-bridge may appear here: the sync engine and its participant take no exception.
#
# path|clause|count|reason
android/messaging/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/messaging/engine/MediaEngineSupport.kt|catch (e: Throwable)|1|Phase 11 design section 6.5/13.7 (slice S5): the media worker thread's boundary converts any preparation failure - including unexpected defects - into the registry's typed CANCELLED state so a preparation never hangs; the worker holds no actor, session or crash-enumeration state an injected Error must reach (unlike the DM actor), and a caught Error here surfaces as the typed failure, not a swallowed crash of the engine
android/media/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/media/sandbox/MediaDecodeService.kt|catch (e: RuntimeException)|2|Phase 11 design section 9.2 (slice S5): the isolated decoding service answers a decoder failure (any ImageDecoder/Bitmap RuntimeException) with a typed refusal so a malformed file cannot wedge a request; an Error (an OOM, a hard crash) is not caught and kills the instance, which is the DeadObjectException path the client handles - the sandbox holds no GHOST state an injected crash must reach, nothing is swallowed
android/messaging/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/messaging/android/ExpiryAlarmReceiver.kt|catch (e: RuntimeException)|1|A-2: releases the goAsync wakelock exactly once if the actor hand-off fails, then rethrows the same exception; no crash is swallowed
android/messaging/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/messaging/engine/DmActor.kt|catch (e: Throwable)|2|runPass records the pass's failure and rethrows it; around schedule.afterCommit() the schedule's own failure is rethrown when the pass succeeded and attached as suppressed to the pass's failure when it did not (S9 review) - nothing is swallowed, an injected crash still reaches the top level
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/DmNative.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|design 2.7: a native library that does not load is DmCode.CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE, reported through isAvailable() and loadFailure(), never an Error escaping into :messaging
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/DmFacade.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|design 2.7: a library that disappeared between the availability check and the call is DmResult.unavailable() (CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE); only this one Error type is caught, so an injected crash passes through
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/MediaNative.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|Phase 11 design §13.2 (slice S2), the DmNative rule: a native library that does not load is MediaCode.CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE, reported through isAvailable() and loadFailure(), never an Error escaping into :messaging
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/MediaCrypto.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|Phase 11 design §13.1/§13.2 (slice S2), the DmFacade rule: a library that disappeared between the availability check and the call is MediaResult.unavailable() (CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE); only this one Error type is caught, so an injected crash passes through
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/MlsNative.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|Phase 10 design 10.1/10.2 (slice S2b), the DmNative rule: a native library that does not load is MlsCode.CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE, reported through isAvailable() and loadFailure(), never an Error escaping into :messaging
android/crypto-bridge/src/main/kotlin/org/ghost/crypto/bridge/ChannelCrypto.kt|catch (e: UnsatisfiedLinkError)|1|Phase 10 design 10.2 (slice S2b), the DmFacade rule: a library that disappeared between the availability check and the call is MlsReply.unavailable() (CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE); only this one Error type is caught, so an injected crash passes through
